  "instruction": "Which authors contributed articles to the NAWE's Writing in Education journal, vol 33 'Writing & Location'?",
  "answer": "Based on the NAWE website, **Writing in Education Vol. 33 \"Writing & Location\"** contains the following articles and authors:\n\n**Article authors (contributors):**\n- **Bryan Podmore** — 2 articles: \"A Risky Business This Writing?\" and \"Crashing through the Fourth Wall\"\n- **Sarah Wardle** — 2 articles: \"Audere Est Facere\" and \"Reflections on Memory and Identity\"\n- **Martin Goodman** — \"Location and Dislocation - a Writer's Use of Place\"\n- **Fred Sedgwick** — \"Primary Children Writing in the Grip of Shakespeare\"\n- **Paul Munden** — \"Text and Context\"\n- **Maggie Butt** — \"The View from Here\"\n- **Keith Bennett** — \"Welcome to Maribor\"\n- **Carl Tighe** — \"Worlds in War: War in Words\" (Inaugural Lecture as Professor of Creative Writing at University of Derby)\n\n**Also featured as respondents** in Podmore's \"A Risky Business This Writing?\": Susan Wicks, Michelene Wandor, Gillian Allnutt, and Graham Mort.\n\n(Note: There's also a **Vol. 31 \"Writing & Location\"** with a different set of authors — Fred Sedgwick, Margaret Anne Clarke, Rupert Loydell, Ade Solanke, Jenny Webb, Hazel Moffat, Mike Ferguson, Fiona Coe, David Orme, Marianne Wheelaghan — but you asked specifically about Vol. 33.)",
